    <TTEXTS:has_summary rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">In this graphic memoir, actor George Takei recounts his childhood experiences in a Japanese American internment camp during World War II. Through his family's story, the book explores themes of injustice, resilience, and the importance of speaking out against prejudice and government abuse.</TTEXTS:has_summary>
